msgid "New text / paragraph:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:339
msgid "New section for `#[export_visibility = …]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:341
msgid ""
"If this RFC is adopted (and stabilized) then https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"reference/abi.html should get a new section:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:360
msgid ""
"Note that the applicability wording proposed above is based on the following "
"factors:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:363
msgid ""
"Desire to only apply the `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute to items for "
"which [`contains_extern_indicator`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"blob/3bc767e1a215c4bf8f099b32e84edb85780591b1/compiler/rustc_middle/src/"
"middle/codegen_fn_attrs.rs#L174-L184) is `true`.  Today this covers:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:367
msgid "All items that use the `#[no_mangle]` attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:368
msgid "All items that use the `#[export_name = ...]` attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:369
msgid "All items that use the `#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]` attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:370
msgid ""
"Some items that use `#[linkage = ...]` (note that this attribute has not yet "
"been [stabilized](https://doc.rust-lang.org/beta/unstable-book/language-"
"features/linkage.html?highlight=linkage#linkage) and this is why it is not "
"yet mentioned in the proposed reference text above)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:375
msgid ""
"Desire to forbid applying the `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute in "
"cases where doing so may increase an item visibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:377
msgid ""
"This is why `#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]` is intentionally omitted and why "
"the RFC proposes that using `#[export_visibility = ...]` for "
"`#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]` items should be an error.  See also the [why-"
"new-attr-cant-increase-visibility](#context-why-the-new-attribute-cannot-"
"increase-visibility) section below."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:382
msgid "Other details"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:384
msgid ""
"Other details (probably not important enough to include in the official "
"reference documentation for Rust):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:387
msgid ""
"The proposal in this RFC has been prototyped in https://github.com/"
"anforowicz/rust/tree/export-visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:392
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:395
msgid "No drawbacks have been identified at this point."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:397
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:400
msgid "Context: why the new attribute cannot increase visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:403
msgid ""
"The `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute may only be applied to item "
"definitions with an \"extern\" indicator as checked by [`fn "
"contains_extern_indicator`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"blob/3bc767e1a215c4bf8f099b32e84edb85780591b1/compiler/rustc_middle/src/"
"middle/codegen_fn_attrs.rs#L174-L184)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:407
msgid ""
"Based on the above, the `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute may never "
"_increase_ visibility of a symbol.  This is because:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:410
msgid ""
"`#[no_mangle]` and `#[export_name = ...]` force the _maximum_ possible "
"visiblity.  See [here](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"blob/8111a2d6da405e9684a8a83c2c9d69036bf23f12/compiler/rustc_monomorphize/"
"src/partitioning.rs#L930-L937)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:413
msgid ""
"It seems that `#[linkage = ...]` should have no impact on symbol visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:414
msgid ""
"One known exception is `#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]` - see [here](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/8111a2d6da405e9684a8a83c2c9d69036bf23f12/"
"compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/symbol_export.rs#L527-L542). The RFC "
"avoids this exception by disallowing using `#[export_visibility = ...]` with "
"`#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:419
msgid "Rationale for not supporting `interposable` visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:421
msgid ""
"The [why-new-attr-cant-increase-visibility](#context-why-the-new-attribute-"
"cannot-increase-visibility) section above means that `#[export_visibility = "
"\"interposable\"]` would be a no-op.  Because of this, the "
"`\"interposable\"` visibility value is not supported by the "
"`#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:426
msgid ""
"Side-note: The \"interposable\" visibility is sometimes called \"default\" "
"\\[linker\\] visibility (see [the LLVM documentation here](https://llvm.org/"
"docs/LangRef.html#visibility-styles)), or \"public\" or \"exported\" "
"visibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:431
msgid ""
"Lack of support for the `\"interposable\"` visibility means that this RFC "
"avoids potential open questions about interaction with "
"`__declspec(dllexport)` and/or whether `rustc` would have to enable the [the "
"LLVM SemanticInterposition feature](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/"
"ClangCommandLineReference.html#cmdoption-clang-fsemantic-interposition)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:436
msgid "Rationale for not requiring `unsafe` when using the new attribute"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:438
msgid "Naming collisions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:440
msgid ""
"The risk of naming collisions is introduced by lack of mangling (e.g. caused "
"by the presence of `#[no_mangle]` or `#[export_name = ...]` attributes).  "
"Presence of `#[export_visibility = ...]` does not _introduce_ this risk."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:445
msgid ""
"The [scope-of-naming-collision-risk](#scope-of-ub-risk) section above points "
"out that symbol visiblity affects the _scope_ of the risk of undefined "
"behavior (UB) stemming from naming collisions.  `#[export_visibility = ...]` "
"never increases this risk, because the [why-new-attr-cant-increase-"
"visibility](#context-why-the-new-attribute-cannot-increase-visibility) "
"section above shows that `#[export_visibility = ...]` can never _increase_ "
"visibility of a symbol."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:451
msgid "Missing symbols"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:453
msgid ""
"The [hidden-vs-dylibs](#interaction-between-export_visibility--hidden-vs-"
"dylibs) section below points out that using `#[export_visibility = ...]` may "
"break `dylib`s.  This concern is tracked as an open question, but this kind "
"of breakage is well-defined and doesn't lead to undefined behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:458
msgid ""
"In particular, it is understood that hiding symbols from `dylib` may result "
"in linking failures (symbol X not found).  This risk is quite similar to the "
"risk of forgetting to write `pub mod` instead of `mod` (and we don't require "
"writing `unsafe mod`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:463
msgid "Alternative: `#[rust_symbol_export_level]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:465
msgid ""
"The `#[export_visibility = ...]` proposed in this RFC supports directly "
"controlling an exact visibility level of a symbol.  One alternative is to "
"control the visibility indirectly, levereging the fact that `#[no_mangle]` "
"and `#[export_name = ...]` symbols are currently public only because:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:470
msgid ""
"Such symbols are treated as `SymbolExportLevel::C`: https://github.com/rust-"
"lang/rust/blob/3048886e59c94470e726ecaaf2add7242510ac11/compiler/"
"rustc_codegen_ssa/src/back/symbol_export.rs#L593-L605"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:472
msgid ""
"`SymbolExportLevel::C` translates into public visibility, but visibility of "
"`SymbolExportLevel::Rust` may be controlled via `-Zdefault-visibility=...`: "
"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"blob/3048886e59c94470e726ecaaf2add7242510ac11/compiler/rustc_monomorphize/"
"src/partitioning.rs#L941-L948"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:477
msgid ""
"Special thanks to @bjorn3 for proposing this alternative in https://github."
"com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3834#issuecomment-2978073435"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:480
msgid ""
"This alternative has been prototyped in https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"commit/9dd4d3f6b2beecb85ff4220502a8c7f61edca839 and tested to verify that it "
"also addresses https://crbug.com/418073233 (with similar test/repro steps as "
"in #comment12 of that bug, but using https://crrev.com/c/6580611/3)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:486
msgid "Other notes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:488
msgid "Pros:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:489
msgid ""
"It is simpler (`#[rust_symbol_export_level]` vs `#[export_visibility = "
"\"<some value>\"]`) both for users and for implementation."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:492
msgid ""
"It avoids some problems and open questions associated with "
"`#[export_visibility = ...]`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:494
msgid ""
"No `dylib` trouble (see [hidden-vs-dylibs](#interaction-between-"
"export_visibility--hidden-vs-dylibs))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:495
msgid ""
"No need to define behavior of specific visibilities - this question is "
"punted to `-Zdefault-visibility=...`. See also \\[cross-platform-behavior\\]."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:498
msgid "Cons:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:499
msgid "Doesn't give the same level of control as C++ attributes"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:500
msgid "Open questions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:501
msgid ""
"The name of the attribute proposed in this alternative is subject to change "
"if a better name is proposed."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:503
msgid "Possible follow-ups (but probably out-of-scope for this RFC):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:504
msgid ""
"@chorman0773 pointed out in https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"pull/3834#issuecomment-2981459636 that an inverse attribute may also be "
"desirable in some scenarios (e.g. `c_symbol_export_level`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:509
msgid "Alternative: version scripts"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:511
msgid ""
"Using [linker version scripts](https://sourceware.org/binutils/docs/ld/"
"VERSION.html) has been proposed as a way to control visibility of Rust-"
"defined symbols (e.g. this is a workaround pointed out in https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/rust/issues/18541). In particular, using version scripts is indeed "
"a feasible way of avoiding undefined behavior from https://crbug."
"com/418073233."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:519
msgid ""
"Using a version script has the following downsides compared to the "
"`#[export_visibility = ...]`\\-based approach proposed in this RFC:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:522
msgid ""
"Using the attribute allows the compiler to optimize the code a bit more than "
"when using a version script (based on [this Stack Overflow answer](https://"
"stackoverflow.com/a/58527480/24042981))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:526
msgid ""
"Using a version script means that visibility of a symbol is defined in a "
"centralized location, far away from the source code of the symbol."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:528
msgid ""
"Copying symbol definitions from `.rs` files into a new library is not "
"sufficient for preserving symbol visibility (for that the version script has "
"to be replicated as well)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:531
msgid ""
"There is a risk that version script and the symbol definition may diverge (e."
"g. after renaming symbol name in an `.rs` file, one has to remember to check "
"if a version script also needs to be updated)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:534
msgid ""
"Version scripts don't work on all target platforms.  In particular, they "
"work in GNU `ld` and LLVM `lld`, but the native Microsoft Visual C++ linker "
"(`link.exe`) does not directly support GNU-style version scripts. Instead, "
"MSVC uses `.def` (module-definition) files to control symbol export and "
"other aspects of DLL creation.  Having to use [a `.def` file](https://learn."
"microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/reference/exports?view=msvc-170) has a few "
"extra downsides compared to a version script:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:541
msgid "Having to support both formats"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:542
msgid ""
"Lack of support for wildcards means that it is impossible to hide all "
"symbols matching a pattern like `*cxxbridge*` used by `cxx` in auto-"
"generated FFI thunks."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:545
msgid ""
"Using a version script is one way of fixing https://crbug.com/418073233. "
"This fix approach requires that authors of each future shared library know "
"about the problem and use a version script.  This is in contrast to using `-"
"Zdefault-visibility=hidden` and `#[export_visibility = \"target_default\"]` "
"for `cxx` symbols, which has to be done only once to centrally, "
"automatically avoid the problem for all `cxx`\\-dependent libraries in a "
"given build environment.  (In fairness, using the command-line flag also "
"requires awareness and opt-in, but it seems easier to append `-Zdefault-"
"visibility=hidden` to default `rustflags` in globally-applicable build "
"settings than it is to modify build tools to require a linker script for all "
"shared libraries.  In fact, Chromium [already builds with the `-Zdefault-"
"visibility=...` flag](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/"
"main:build/config/gcc/BUILD.gn;l=34-35;"
"drc=ee3900fd57b3c580aefff15c64052904d81b7760).)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:558
msgid "Alternative: introduce `-Zdefault-visibility-for-c-exports=...`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:560
msgid ""
"Introducing and using `-Zdefault-visibility-for-c-export=hidden` can realize "
"most benefits outlined in the \"Motivation\" section (except C/C++ parity). "
"In particular this is a feasible way of avoiding undefined behavior from "
"https://crbug.com/418073233."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:566
msgid ""
"The main downside, is that it doesn't support making a subset of Rust-"
"defined symbols public, while hiding another subset.  This may still be "
"achievable, but would require reaching out for C/C++ to export some symbols "
"(i.e. defining `foo_hidden` in Rust, and then calling it from a publicly "
"exported `foo` defined in C/C++)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:572
msgid ""
"Alternative: change behavior of `#[no_mangle]` in future language edition"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:574
msgid ""
"Some past proposals suggested changing the behavior of `#[no_mangle]` (and "
"`#[export_name = ...]`) attribute in a future Rust language edition. For "
"example, this is what has been proposed in https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/73958#issuecomment-2889126604 (although it seems that this proposal "
"wouldn't help with https://crbug.com/418073233, because it seems to only "
"affect scenarios where linking is driven by `rustc`). Other edition-boundary "
"changes may also be considered - for example just changing the default "
"effect of `#[no_mangle]` from (pseudo-code) `#[export_visibility = "
"\"interposable\"]` to `#[export_visibility = \"target_default\"]` (which "
"combined with `-Zdefault-visibility=hidden` should address https://crbug."
"com/418073233)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:588
msgid ""
"It seems that the new edition behaviors proposed above would still benefit "
"from having a way to diverge from the default visibility behavior of "
"`#[no_mangle]` symbols.  And therefore it seems that the "
"`#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute proposed in this RFC would be useful "
"not only in the current Rust edition, but also in the hypothetical future "
"Rust edition."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:594
msgid "Rationale: Okay to have no impact on Rust standard library"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:596
msgid ""
"This RFC treats visibility of Rust standard library symbols as out of scope. "
"`-Zdefault-visibility=...` remains the only way to control symbol visibility "
"of the Rust standard library (assumming that it can be rebuilt with this "
"command-line flag).  This is ok - the RFC is beneficial even with this "
"limited scope."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:602
msgid ""
"More details about symbols exported from the Rust standard library can be "
"found in the folded details section below:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:607
msgid "Symbols exported from Rust standard library"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:609
msgid ""
"Currently Rust standard library may end up exporting two kinds of symbols. "
"One kind is symbols using `#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]` attribute (similar "
"to `#[no_mangle]` so in theory `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute could "
"be applied to such symbols). An example can be found below:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:630
msgid ""
"But non-`#[rustc_std_internal_symbol]` symbols (e.g. [`String::new`](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/9c4ff566babe632af5e30281a822d1ae9972873b/"
"library/alloc/src/string.rs#L439-L446)) can also end up publicly exported:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:646
msgid ""
"**Disclaimer**: The example above could be illustrated with other crates. It "
"uses `llguidance` because:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:649
msgid ""
"it exposes C API (and therefore it is potentially useful to build it as a "
"`staticlib`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:651
msgid ""
"it happens to be used by Chromium so the RFC author is somewhat familiar "
"with the crate"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:653
msgid ""
"the RFC author had trouble building `rustc-demangle-capi` in this way "
"(hitting `#[panic_handler]`\\-related errors)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:656
msgid "Justification for relying on `-Zdefault-visibility=...`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:658
msgid ""
"Symbols can be hidden by rebuilding Rust standard library with `-Zdefault-"
"visibility=hidden`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:661
msgid ""
"There are other valid reasons for rebuilding the standard library when "
"building a given project. For example this is a way to use globally "
"consistent `-C` options like `-Cpanic=abort`, [`-Clto=no`](https://source."
"chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn;"
"l=1115-1118;drc=26d51346374a0d16b0ba2243ef83c015a944d975), etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:668
msgid ""
"Rebuilding the standard library is possible, although it is currently "
"supported as an **unstable** [`-Zbuild-std`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/"
"reference/unstable.html#build-std) command-line flag of `cargo`. FWIW "
"Chromium currently does rebuild the standard library (using automated "
"[tooling](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:tools/"
"rust/gnrt_stdlib.py;drc=628c608971bc01c96193055bb0848149cccde645) to "
"translate standard library's `Cargo.toml` files into [equivalent `BUILD.gn` "
"rules](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:build/rust/"
"std/rules/BUILD.gn;drc=35fb76c686b55acc25b53f7e5c9b58e56dca7f4a)), which is "
"one reason why this RFC is a viable UB fix for https://crbug.com/418073233."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:682
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:685
msgid "Other languages"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:687
msgid ""
"This RFC is quite directly based on how C/C++ supports per-item "
"`__attribute__ ((visibility (\"default\")))` (at least in [Clang](https://"
"clang.llvm.org/docs/AttributeReference.html#visibility) and [GCC](https://"
"gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Common-Function-Attributes.html#index-visibility-"
"function-attribute)). Using an assembly language, one can also use the `."
"hidden` directive (e.g. see [here](https://docs.oracle.com/cd/E26502_01/html/"
"E28388/eoiyg.html#:~:text=.hidden%20symbol1%2C%20symbol2%2C%20..."
"%2C%20symbolN))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:696
msgid ""
"It seems that so far a similar feature hasn't yet been introduced to other "
"languages that compile to native binary code:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:699
msgid ""
"It is unclear if GoLang has a way to explicitly specify visibility. Using "
"`#pragma GCC visibility push(hidden)` has been proposed as a workaround (see "
"[here](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/28340#issuecomment-466645246))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:703
msgid ""
"Haskell libraries can say `foreign export ccall some_function_name :: Int -> "
"Int` to export a function (see [the Haskell wiki](https://wiki.haskell.org/"
"Foreign_Function_Interface)). Presumably such functions are publicly "
"exported (just as with Rust's `#[no_mangle]`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:709
msgid ""
"There is [a proposal](https://forums.swift.org/t/current-status-of-swift-"
"symbol-visibility/66949) for Swift language to leverage [the `package` "
"access modifier](https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-evolution/blob/main/"
"proposals/0386-package-access-modifier.md) as a way to specify public "
"visibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:714
msgid ""
"There is an open issue that tracks adding a similar mechanism to Zig: "
"https://github.com/ziglang/zig/issues/9762"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:717
msgid "Rust language"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:719
msgid ""
"[`#[linkage...]` attribute](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/29603) "
"has been proposed in the past for specifying [linkage type](https://llvm.org/"
"docs/LangRef.html#linkage-types) of a symbol (e.g. `weak`, `linkonce_odr`, "
"etc.). Linkage type is related to, but nevertheless different from [linkage "
"visibility](https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#visibility-styles) that this "
"RFC focuses on."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:727
msgid ""
"The `#[export_visibility = ...]` attribute has been earlier covered by a "
"Major Change Proposal (MCP) at https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-team/"
"issues/881, but it was pointed out that \"a compiler MCP isn't quite the "
"right avenue here, as attributes are part of the language.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:734
msgid "Unresolved questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:737
msgid "There are no unresolved questions at this point."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:739
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:742
msgid "Provide reference-level definitions of supported visibility levels"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:744
msgid ""
"`#[export = \"target_default\"]` defers the choice of an actual visibility "
"level to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:747
msgid ""
"Session-wide default of [`SymbolVisibility::Interposable`](https://github."
"com/rust-lang/rust/blob/910617d84d611e9ba508fd57a058c59b8a767697/compiler/"
"rustc_session/src/session.rs#L551-L557)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:749
msgid ""
"Unless overridden by target platform’s default visibility specified in "
"[`rustc_target::spec::TargetOptions`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"blob/910617d84d611e9ba508fd57a058c59b8a767697/compiler/rustc_target/src/spec/"
"mod.rs#L2225-L2230),"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:751
msgid ""
"Or overridden by [`-Zdefault-visibility=...`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/beta/"
"unstable-book/compiler-flags/default-visibility.html) command-line flag."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:755
msgid ""
"This means that _this_ RFC doesn't necessarily need to define the exact "
"semantics and behavior of supported visibility levels. OTOH, such "
"definitions may be desirable in the future:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:759
msgid "If/when stabilizing `-Zdefault-visibility=...`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:760
msgid ""
"If/when extending `#[export_visibility = ...]` to support specific "
"visibility levels (i.e. if the attribute would support not only the "
"`\"target_default\"` visibility value, but also `\"hidden\"`, "
"`\"protected\"`, and/or `\"interposable\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:765
msgid ""
"One way to provide such definitions would be to map different visibility "
"levels into specific behavior on the supported Tier 1 platforms.   This can "
"be limited to documenting the impact for ELF, Mach-O, and PE binaries, "
"because all of [Tier 1 target triples](https://doc.rust-lang.org/beta/rustc/"
"platform-support.html#tier-1-with-host-tools) use one of those three binary "
"formats:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:771
msgid ""
"`aarch64-apple-darwin`: MachO (documented [here](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"beta/rustc/platform-support/apple-darwin.html#binary-format))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:773
msgid ""
"`aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`: PE/COFF (documented [here](https://doc.rust-lang."
"org/beta/rustc/platform-support/windows-msvc.html#platform-details))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:775
msgid "`aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`: ELF"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:776
msgid "`i686-pc-windows-msvc`: PE/COFF (same documentation as above)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:777
msgid "`i686-unknown-linux-gnu`: ELF"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:778
msgid ""
"`x86_64-pc-windows-gnu`: PE (documented [here](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"beta/rustc/platform-support/windows-gnu.html#requirements))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:780
msgid "`x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`: ELF"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:782
msgid ""
"Ad-hoc, manual tests (e.g. see [here](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"pull/3834#issuecomment-3403039933)) of `#[export_visibility = "
"\"target_default\"]` provide some reassurance that such definitions should "
"be possible in the future. OTOH, when future RFCs or PRs consider "
"implementing specific visibility levels, they should ideally come with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:789
msgid ""
"Codegen tests that verify how `#[export_visibility = …]` is translated into "
"LLVM syntax"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:791
msgid ""
"End-to-end tests for 3 platforms that cover ELF, Mach-O, and PE binaries. "
"Verification in such tests would most likely have to depend on arbitrary "
"developer tools (e.g. [`readelf`](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/"
"readelf.1.html) or [`dumpbin`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/"
"reference/dumpbin-reference?view=msvc-170)) and therefore such tests would "
"most likely have to be `make`\\-based."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:799
msgid "Support hidden visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:801
msgid ""
"In the future, we may consider supporting `#[export_visibility = “hidden”]`. "
"In terms of the internal `rustc` APIs this would map to [`rustc_target::"
"spec::SymbolVisibility::Hidden`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"blob/910617d84d611e9ba508fd57a058c59b8a767697/compiler/rustc_target/src/spec/"
"mod.rs#L884). The hidden visibility would have the following impact on Tier "
"1 binaries:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:806
msgid ""
"ELF binaries: The symbol is marked [`STV_HIDDEN`](https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man5/elf.5.html#:~:text=specific%20hidden%20class.-,STV_HIDDEN,-"
"Symbol%20is%20unavailable)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:808
msgid ""
"PE binaries: The symbol is non-exported (i.e. the symbol is not listed in "
"[the `.edata` section](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/"
"pe-format#the-edata-section-image-only))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:810
msgid ""
"MachO binaries: The symbol is non-exported (i.e. the symbol is not listed in "
"[the export trie](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/"
"blob/8d741a5de7ff4191bf97d57b9f54c2f6d4a15585/EXTERNAL_HEADERS/mach-o/loader."
"h#L1369))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:813
msgid "Open question: `#[export_visibility = \"hidden\"]` vs `dylib`s"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:816
msgid "Problem description"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:818
msgid ""
"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/73958#issuecomment-2635015556 "
"points out that using `#[export_visibility = \"hidden\"]` may break some "
"`dylib` scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:822
msgid ""
"For example, let's say that a crate named `rlib` is compiled into an `rlib` "
"with the following functions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:826
msgid ""
"/// Let's say that this is an internal helper that is only intended to be "
"called\n"
"/// from code within this library.  To facilitate this, this function is "
"*not*\n"
"/// `pub`.\n"
"///\n"
"/// To also enable calling the helper from a friendly (also internal-only),\n"
"/// supporting C/C++ library we may use `#[no_mangle]`.  To keep this "
"function\n"
"/// internal and only enable directly calling this helper from statically-"
"linked\n"
"/// C/C++ libraries we may /// use `#[export_visibility = \"hidden\"]`.  We "
"will\n"
"/// see below how the hidden visibility may have some undesirable\n"
"/// interactions with `dylib`s.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:837
msgid "\"hidden\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:839
msgid ""
"/// This is a public (`pub`) Rust function - it may be called from other "
"Rust\n"
"/// crates.\n"
"///\n"
"/// This function may internally (say, as an implementation detail) call\n"
"/// `fn internal_helper_called_from_rust_or_cpp` above.  If this public "
"function\n"
"/// gets inlined into another `dylib` then the call to the internal helper\n"
"/// will cross `dylib` boundaries - this will **not** work if the internal\n"
"/// helper is hidden from dynamic linking.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:854
msgid "Potential answers"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:856
msgid ""
"The following options have been identified so far as a potential way for "
"answering the `dylib`\\-vs-`hidden`\\-visibility problem:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:859
msgid ""
"Don't stabilize `#[export_visibility = \"hidden\"]` (initially? forever?)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:860
msgid "Support `#[export_visibility = \"hidden\"]`, but"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:861
msgid ""
"Document that `hidden` visibility may break linking of `dylib`s (see the "
"\"Hidden visibility\" section in the guide-level explanation above)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:863
msgid ""
"Document a recommendation that reusable crates shouldn't use a hardcoded "
"visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:865
msgid ""
"Avoid inlining if the inlined code ends up calling a hidden symbol from "
"another `dylib`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:867
msgid ""
"Currently preventing inlining is problematic, because `#[inline]` will stop "
"the function from being codegened in the original crate unless used (hattip "
"[@chorman0773](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"pull/3834#issuecomment-3352655525)). OTOH, this doesn't necessarily seem "
"like a hard blocker (i.e. maybe this behavior can change)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:873
msgid ""
"Generics also cannot have code generated in the original crate, because "
"codegen requires knowing the generic parameters.  But generics seem "
"irrelevant here, because `#[export_visibility = ...]` does _not_ apply to "
"generics.  In particular, `#[no_mangle]` ([Rust playground](https://play."
"rust-lang.org/?"
"version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=ac8f26f9b05471c2480b3185388c05e8)) "
"and `#[export_name = ...]` cannot be used with generics, because the names "
"of the symbols (ones generated during monomorphization) need to differ based "
"on the generic parameters."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:882
msgid ""
"One major problem with avoiding inlining is that during codegen it is not "
"yet known if two crates will end up getting linked into the same or "
"different dylib.  This means that inlining would need to be inhibited for "
"any cross-crate calls into hidden symbols.  And this would suppress many "
"legitimate optimizations. (hattip [@bjorn3](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rfcs/pull/3834#issuecomment-3352658642))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:888
msgid ""
"Add a lint/warning that detects when `#[export_visibility = ...]` is used "
"inappropriately"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:890
msgid ""
"Sub-idea 1: when a hidden function is called from a caller that may be "
"inlined into another crate.  (hattip [@tmandry](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rfcs/pull/3834#issuecomment-3282373591))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:893
msgid ""
"This idea is problematic, because using inlineability for restricting how "
"source programs are written means committing to implementation details of "
"rustc’s codegen strategy.  For example, `rustc` currently has some logic to "
"treat small functions as-if they were `#[inline]` for codegen purposes even "
"if they weren’t declared as such in the source code. (hattip [@hanna-kruppe]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3834#discussion_r2395437679))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:900
msgid ""
"Sub-idea 2: when a hidden function is called _at all_ from another Rust "
"function"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:902
msgid ""
"This seems very drastic, but in practice `#[no_mangle]` are oftentimes "
"called only from _another, non-Rust_ language.  This is definitely the case "
"for FFI thunks used as one of motivating examples in this RFC."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:906
msgid "Support protected visibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:908
msgid ""
"In the future, we may consider supporting `#[export_visibility = "
"“protected”]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:910
msgid "Open question:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3834-export-visibility.md:912
msgid ""
"Need to clarify how `protected` vs `interposable` visibilities would work "
"for Tier 1 platforms.  In particular, it seems that PE and Mach-O binary "
"formats may not be able to distinguish between `protected` and "
"`interposable` visibilities (the latter is the default when a `#[no_mangle]` "
"symbol is not accompanied by `#[export_visibility = ...]`)."
msgstr ""
